{"verdict": "revise",
  "hypothesis_status": {"H1": "refuted", "H2": "supported", "H3": "supported"},
  "issues": [
    "C1/E1 failed due to SQL column error; no evidence was produced for H1. The ground-truth facts directly contradict H1's claim that NWM 'fails to capture the hydropeaking pulse on days when its analysis/assimilation cycle does not include the pulse hour (Oct 18–22)'. NWM has NO DATA for Oct 18–22 CDT (coverage starts Oct 23 2 AM CDT). Missing data ≠ model failure; those days cannot be evaluated. On the two evaluable days (Oct 23–24), ground-truth shows NWM peaks +1 h lag and magnitude errors of -241 cfs (Oct 23) and -112 cfs (Oct 24), not the claimed ~200–500 cfs underestimate.",
    "C2/E2 misreads the data: the rows show multiple hours per day (hours 2–7 on Oct 18 with peaks 676–702 cfs), not the daily maximum 15-min peak. Ground-truth facts confirm the daily USGS 15-min peak occurs at 21:00 CDT on Oct 18–22 (8,180; 7,990; 5,340; 7,100; 5,640 cfs) and shifts to 19:00 CDT on Oct 23–24 (5,640; 5,220 cfs). This consistent recurrence at a fixed local hour (21:00 then 19:00) with zero rain strongly supports H2's claim of scheduled hydropower releases. C2's 'refutes' stance is wrong; H2 is supported.",
    "C3/E3 correctly confirms USGS and NWS Oliver tailwater stages are identical (stage_diff_ft ≤ 0.04 ft), proving the same physical sensor. The daily mean gap (NWS ~1,104 cfs vs USGS ~800 cfs over 7 days) is a rating-curve discrepancy, not a stage measurement error. H3 is supported.",
    "Critical gap: No check has quantified NWM performance on Oct 23–24 (the only days with NWM data) against the USGS 15-min peak and hourly mean at the surge hour and surrounding hours. This is needed to properly evaluate H1's timing and magnitude claims."
  ],
  "new_checks": [
    {"id": "C4", "hypothesis": "H1", "purpose": "Quantify NWM vs USGS on the two days NWM has data (Oct 23–24 CDT): extract the USGS 15-min peak hour, NWM peak hour and value in a ±4 h window, and the NWM value at the USGS peak hour, to verify the +1 h lag and magnitude error.", "how": "WITH usgs_peaks AS (SELECT to_date(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago')) AS local_day, hr_utc AS usgs_peak_hr_utc, usgs_northport_peak_cfs AS usgs_peak_cfs FROM water.hourly_compare WHERE hr_utc BETWEEN '2026-10-23 00:00' AND '2026-10-25 06:00' AND usgs_northport_peak_cfs IS NOT NULL QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY to_date(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago')) ORDER BY usgs_northport_peak_cfs DESC) = 1) SELECT u.local_day, hour(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(u.usgs_peak_hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago')) AS usgs_peak_hr_cdt, u.usgs_peak_cfs, n.hr_utc AS nwm_peak_hr_utc, hour(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(n.hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago')) AS nwm_peak_hr_cdt, n.nwm_cfs AS nwm_peak_cfs, (hour(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(n.hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago')) - hour(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(u.usgs_peak_hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago'))) AS lag_hours, (n.nwm_cfs - u.usgs_peak_cfs) AS magnitude_error_cfs, n_at_peak.nwm_cfs AS nwm_at_usgs_peak_cfs FROM usgs_peaks u JOIN water.hourly_compare n ON n.hr_utc BETWEEN date_sub(u.usgs_peak_hr_utc, 4) AND date_add(u.usgs_peak_hr_utc, 4) AND n.nwm_cfs IS NOT NULL QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY u.local_day ORDER BY n.nwm_cfs DESC) = 1 LEFT JOIN water.hourly_compare n_at_peak ON n_at_peak.hr_utc = u.usgs_peak_hr_utc ORDER BY u.local_day"},
    {"id": "C5", "hypothesis": "H2", "purpose": "Extract the exact CDT hour of the daily maximum 15-min peak (usgs_northport_peak_cfs) for each full local day Oct 18–24 to confirm the consistent 21:00 CDT recurrence on Oct 18–22 and shift to 19:00 CDT on Oct 23–24.", "how": "SELECT to_date(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago')) AS local_day, hour(from_utc_timestamp(to_timestamp(hr_utc, 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm'), 'America/Chicago')) AS peak_hour_cdt, MAX(usgs_northport_peak_cfs) AS max_peak_cfs FROM water.hourly_compare WHERE hr_utc BETWEEN '2026-10-18 06:00' AND '2026-10-25 06:00' AND usgs_northport_peak_cfs IS NOT NULL GROUP BY local_day, peak_hour_cdt QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY local_day ORDER BY MAX(usgs_northport_peak_cfs) DESC) = 1 ORDER BY local_day"}
  ]}
